    FEATURE-004 Asset Management - AM-005 Asset Modification Wizard Views
    =====================================================================

    Provides the form view and window action for the TransientModel
    ``account.asset.modification.wizard``.  Supports five modification
    types in accordance with IAS 16 (Property, Plant and Equipment),
    IAS 36 (Impairment of Assets), and US GAAP ASC 360:

      * ``revaluation``          - value increase posted to equity
                                   revaluation surplus (IAS 16 revaluation
                                   model; credit revaluation reserve).
      * ``impairment``           - value decrease posted to expense
                                   impairment loss (IAS 36 / ASC 360;
                                   debit impairment loss expense).
      * ``impairment_reversal``  - partial reversal of a prior impairment
                                   where recoverable amount has risen;
                                   limited to the original impairment or
                                   the depreciated historical cost,
                                   whichever is lower.
      * ``useful_life_change``   - extend or reduce remaining useful life
                                   with automatic depreciation schedule
                                   recalculation on confirmation.
      * ``salvage_change``       - adjust salvage/residual value; final
                                   NBV still converges to salvage at the
                                   end of useful life.

    Each modification type applies GAAP/IFRS-compliant journal entries
    and triggers depreciation recalculation on the underlying asset.

    The form is opened from the Asset form's header "Modify" button via
    ``account.asset.action_modify()``, which returns this action.  The
    action also binds to the ``account.asset`` model so that it surfaces
    in the Action menu on asset records (contextual action).

    AAP Rule Compliance
    ===================
    * R-01 (Module independence) - No references to sibling CE modules
      (account_budget_management, account_deferred_revenue,
      account_payment_followup).  Only references this module's model
      ``account.asset.modification.wizard`` (net-new TransientModel),
      ``account.asset`` (same module, net-new), and core Odoo models
      (``account.move``, ``account.account``, ``res.company``,
      ``res.currency``, ``base.group_multi_company``).
    * R-02 (No Enterprise deps) - No references to Enterprise modules
      in any field, action, or attribute.
    * R-05 (No core view modification) - This file defines NET-NEW views
      on a NET-NEW TransientModel; NO ``inherit_id`` attribute appears
      on any record.
    * R-07 (No sudo) - Not applicable; XML-only data file.
    * R-09 (Exact module folder name) - File lives in
      ``addons/account_asset_management/views/`` as required.

    Odoo 19.0 View Conventions Observed
    ===================================
    * ``invisible="expression"`` and ``readonly="expression"`` attributes
      (NOT ``attrs="..."``) per Odoo 17+ convention.
    * Boolean / comparison operators: ``and``, ``or``, ``not``, ``in``,
      ``not in``; comparisons use XML-escaped ``&gt;``, ``&lt;``, ``&amp;``.
    * 4-space indentation throughout.
    * ``<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>`` header.
-->
<odoo>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         WIZARD FORM VIEW
         ==================================================================
         The single form view for the ``account.asset.modification.wizard``
         TransientModel.  Displays the target asset, modification type,
         and modification-specific input groups (value adjustment, useful
         life change, or salvage change).  After posting, the generated
         journal entry is linked for drill-through.

         Conditional visibility is driven by ``modification_type`` and
         ``state`` so that the wizard adapts to each of the five
         modification types without overwhelming the user with irrelevant
         fields.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="view_account_asset_modification_wizard_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.asset.modification.wizard.form</field>
        <field name="model">account.asset.modification.wizard</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form string="Modify Asset">
                <!-- HEADER: state statusbar only. Action buttons live
                     in the <footer> block so Odoo suppresses the default
                     Save/Discard wizard buttons (Issue #5 fix). The
                     state field stays in the header so the statusbar
                     widget renders at the top of the form. -->
                <header>
                    <field name="state"
                           widget="statusbar"
                           statusbar_visible="draft,confirmed,posted"/>
                </header>
                <sheet>
                    <!-- PRIMARY GROUP: Asset + Modification metadata.
                         Two-column layout.  Left: asset and company context.
                         Right: modification type and effective date. -->
                    <group>
                        <group string="Asset">
                            <field name="asset_id"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"
                                   options="{'no_create': True, 'no_open': False}"/>
                            <field name="company_id"
                                   groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
                            <field name="currency_id" invisible="1"/>
                        </group>
                        <group string="Modification">
                            <field name="modification_type"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                            <field name="effective_date"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                        </group>
                    </group>

                    <!-- VALUE ADJUSTMENT GROUP (conditional).
                         Shown for revaluation, impairment, and impairment
                         reversal.  Displays the previous value (current NBV),
                         the proposed new value, and the computed amount
                         delta with colour-coded decorations:
                             green  = increase (revaluation / reversal)
                             red    = decrease (impairment) -->
                    <group string="Value Adjustment"
                           invisible="modification_type not in ('revaluation', 'impairment', 'impairment_reversal')">
                        <group>
                            <field name="previous_value"/>
                            <field name="new_value"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                        </group>
                        <group>
                            <field name="modification_amount"
                                   decoration-success="modification_amount &gt; 0"
                                   decoration-danger="modification_amount &lt; 0"/>
                        </group>
                    </group>

                    <!-- USEFUL LIFE CHANGE GROUP (conditional).
                         Shown only when modification_type is
                         'useful_life_change'.  The shared previous_value
                         field is relabeled to "Current Remaining Months"
                         so the same underlying field is contextualised per
                         modification type without requiring separate
                         storage columns. -->
                    <group string="Useful Life Change"
                           invisible="modification_type != 'useful_life_change'">
                        <field name="previous_value"
                               string="Current Remaining Months"/>
                        <field name="new_useful_life_months"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- SALVAGE VALUE CHANGE GROUP (conditional).
                         Shown only when modification_type is
                         'salvage_change'.  The shared previous_value
                         field is relabeled to "Current Salvage Value". -->
                    <group string="Salvage Value Change"
                           invisible="modification_type != 'salvage_change'">
                        <field name="previous_value"
                               string="Current Salvage Value"/>
                        <field name="new_salvage_value"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- ACCOUNTING ENTRIES GROUP (conditional).
                         Per IAS 16 / IAS 36 / ASC 360 account-type rules:
                           * revaluation         -> equity revaluation
                                                    surplus (credit)
                           * impairment          -> expense impairment loss
                                                    (debit)
                           * impairment_reversal -> income impairment
                                                    reversal gain (credit)
                         Each field is individually visible based on its
                         modification type; ``no_create: True`` prevents
                         accidental inline account creation since the
                         correct accounts must already be configured. -->
                    <group string="Accounting Entries">
                        <field name="revaluation_surplus_account_id"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"
                               invisible="modification_type != 'revaluation'"
                               options="{'no_create': True}"/>
                        <field name="impairment_loss_account_id"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"
                               invisible="modification_type != 'impairment'"
                               options="{'no_create': True}"/>
                        <field name="impairment_reversal_account_id"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"
                               invisible="modification_type != 'impairment_reversal'"
                               options="{'no_create': True}"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- JUSTIFICATION & DOCUMENTATION GROUP.
                         Per AM-005 Scenario 5 (complete audit trail), the
                         reason text is required and the supporting
                         document attachment (appraisal, impairment
                         assessment) is captured on the wizard and
                         persisted via the audit trail on the underlying
                         asset.

                         Binary widget pair: ``supporting_document``
                         (Binary, attachment=True on the wizard model) is
                         accompanied by its mandatory filename companion
                         ``supporting_document_filename`` (Char, invisible)
                         per Odoo's standard Binary-field convention. -->
                    <group string="Justification &amp; Supporting Documentation">
                        <field name="reason"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"
                               placeholder="Required: reason for modification (e.g., external appraisal, impairment indicators)..."/>
                        <field name="supporting_document"
                               filename="supporting_document_filename"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                        <field name="supporting_document_filename"
                               invisible="1"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- POSTED JOURNAL ENTRY GROUP (post-state only).
                         After successful posting, displays a read-only
                         link to the generated ``account.move`` for
                         drill-through audit.  ``no_create: True`` prevents
                         accidental creation; ``no_open: False`` keeps the
                         "open record" icon enabled. -->
                    <group string="Posted Journal Entry"
                           invisible="state != 'posted'">
                        <field name="move_id"
                               readonly="1"
                               options="{'no_create': True, 'no_open': False}"/>
                    </group>
                </sheet>
                <!-- FOOTER: action buttons. Placing them in <footer>
                     suppresses Odoo's default Save/Discard wizard
                     buttons that would otherwise appear at the bottom
                     of the modal (Issue #5 fix). Each button is gated
                     on the wizard state machine:
                         draft     -> Confirm / Cancel
                         confirmed -> Post Modification / Cancel
                         posted    -> Close (terminal)
                         cancelled -> Close (terminal) -->
                <footer>
                    <button name="action_confirm"
                            string="Confirm"
                            type="object"
                            class="btn-primary"
                            invisible="state != 'draft'"
                            data-hotkey="q"/>
                    <button name="action_post"
                            string="Post Modification"
                            type="object"
                            class="btn-primary"
                            invisible="state != 'confirmed'"
                            data-hotkey="q"/>
                    <button name="action_cancel"
                            string="Cancel"
                            type="object"
                            class="btn-secondary"
                            invisible="state in ('posted', 'cancelled')"/>
                    <button special="cancel"
                            string="Close"
                            class="btn-secondary"
                            invisible="state not in ('posted', 'cancelled')"
                            data-hotkey="z"/>
                    <button special="cancel"
                            string="Discard"
                            class="btn-secondary"
                            invisible="state in ('posted', 'cancelled')"
                            data-hotkey="z"/>
                </footer>
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         WINDOW ACTION
         ==================================================================
         Opens the modification wizard as a modal dialog (``target="new"``).
         Two entry points:
             1. From the asset form's header "Modify" button, where the
                Python method ``account.asset.action_modify()`` returns
                this action with the asset_id pre-populated via context.
             2. From the Action menu on asset records (contextual action)
                via the ``binding_model_id`` reference.

         The model technical id ``model_account_asset`` is Odoo's
         canonical ``ir.model`` record id, auto-generated from the model
         name ``account.asset`` (dots replaced with underscores, prefixed
         with ``model_``).  This id is already referenced by the module's
         ``security/ir.model.access.csv``, confirming it exists after
         ``account.asset`` is registered at module load time.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="action_account_asset_modification_wizard"
            model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Modify Asset</field>
        <field name="res_model">account.asset.modification.wizard</field>
        <field name="view_mode">form</field>
        <field name="view_id"
               ref="view_account_asset_modification_wizard_form"/>
        <field name="target">new</field>
        <field name="binding_model_id" ref="model_account_asset"/>
        <field name="binding_view_types">form</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
